cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Quantum Computing Approaches to Quantum Thermalization in NISQ Devices: Companion Code"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Arroyo Moro"
    given-names: "Enrique"
version: "0.1.0"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  Companion research code for the MSc thesis "Quantum Computing Approaches to
  Quantum Thermalization in NISQ Devices". The repository implements a
  small-system workflow for Markovian open quantum dynamics: construction of
  finite-time Lindblad channels, Choi/Kraus extraction, branch-resolved
  Sz.-Nagy dilation circuits, and reconstruction of observables from simulator,
  fake-backend, and saved IBM Quantum results.
keywords:
  - "open quantum systems"
  - "quantum thermalization"
  - "Lindblad dynamics"
  - "quantum channels"
  - "Kraus representation"
  - "Sz.-Nagy dilation"
  - "NISQ"
  - "Qiskit"
